title: "fix(txpool): handle AlreadyImported race in fork-aware submit_and_watch"

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |
    Fixes a race condition in the fork-aware transaction pool where
    `submit_and_watch` can spuriously return `AlreadyImported` (RPC error 1013)
    even though only a single submission was made. This happens when a concurrent
    `maintain()` call imports the transaction from mempool into a newly-built view
    before `submit_and_watch` gets to submit to that view. When no active view
    accepts the transaction and the resulting error is `AlreadyImported`, it means
    the transaction is already in the pool. Without the fix, this error propagates
    to the RPC caller and the transaction is removed from mempool, degrading its
    persistence. With the fix, `AlreadyImported` is treated as success.

crates:
- name: sc-transaction-pool
  bump: major
